  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Qatar Chamber of Commerce and Industry (QCCI) holds a unique position as the legally mandated national representative of the private sector. Building on QCCI&#x2019;s strong institutional position, extensive membership base, and advanced service infrastructure, the programme will enhance evidence based policy engagement on labour regulation, workforce nationalization (Qatarization), skills development, and enterprise compliance with international labour standards. Particular attention will be given to supporting employers, specially SMEs, in implementing responsible business practices, including fair recruitment, working conditions, grievance mechanisms, and occupational safety and health. The programme will also respond to the indirect effects of regional geopolitical tensions, including the Iran&#x2013;Israel&#x2013;United States conflict, which may affect trade, costs, and labour market stability. Through targeted capacity development, QCCI will be better positioned to contribute constructively to policy dialogue and to support sustainable, inclusive private sector growth.</narrative>
  </description>
